2.36.m:
By the grace of the ocean of compassion he attains spotless knowledge;
Then he reaches supreme peace, the essence of essences, higher than the highest.
In whichever body in Bhārata he receives that mantra, that body is his last.

In the womb, they all remember the deeds arising from hundreds of births;
having emerged from the womb, the soul indeed forgets through Viṣṇu's māyā.
Whether a god or a worm, it protects its body with care. // 129

2.37.m:
A gift to a brāhmaṇa on an ordinary day yields an ordinary fruit;
on a new moon and on a solar transition, the fruit is a hundred times greater;
and on a full moon during Cāturmāsya, it yields an infinite fruit indeed.

2.39.m:
‘oṃ śrīṃ hrīṃ klīṃ aiṃ kamalavāsinyai svāhā.’
By means of this mantra, Kubera attained all sovereignty;
So did the emperor Dakṣa and Sāvarṇi Manu. (45)

Afflicted with sorrow for a very long time, the gods wandered about due to the brāhmaṇa's curse;
afterwards they obtained that Lakṣmī by the boon of Hari, O sage."
The episode of Śrī Lakṣmī is concluded.
